                <pb facs="0326" n="294" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v10/pg294"/>

                <head>146. Telegram From the Commander in Chief, Atlantic (Dennison) to the
                    Commander of Special Task Group 81.8 (Clark)<anchor n="0" xml:id="d146-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Norfolk</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1961-04-19T11:32:00-05:00">April 19, 1961,
                            11:32 a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>191632Z. Bumpy Road. Exclusive for RAdm Clark info Gen Gray from Dennison.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Provide continuous air cover over beaches today to protect CEF from air
                        attack.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Protection from ground attack not authorized.<anchor n="1"
                            xml:id="d146-f2"/></item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d146-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d146-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Naval Historical Center, Area Files, Bumpy Road Materials. Top Secret;
                    Emergency; Exclusive. Repeated to JCS.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d146-f2" n="1" xml:id="d146-f2-content">
                <p>At 11:31 a.m., Clark reported to Dennison that he had received the following
                    message from Blue Beach: “Out of ammunition. Men fighting in water. If no help
                    given Blue Beach lost.” (CTG 81.8 telegram 191631Z to CINCLANTFLT, April 19;
                    ibid.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
